{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdY7SuV5KYijW8Jji1tk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anthropic announced a set of reporting tools on Wednesday that let managers see what a team's Claude Code spending produced. Using internal analytics and employee surveys, a manager can pick a date range and view what the team produced, what it cost, and where its workflows broke down. The reports also offer recommendations for improving results. Anthropic is adding pooled group budgets for token spend as well, and says it won't use this data for model training by default.\n\nThe timing lines up with a data point from Jellyfish, which makes tools for software developers. Its new report on agentic coding tools, based on use by 276,000 of its customers, found that Claude Code and other tools built on Anthropic models account for nearly a third of all proposed code changes submitted for review. Spending on those tools has grown 10x since the start of the year and now equals about 2% of total engineering cost. Jellyfish chief scientist Nicholas Arcolano pointed out that 2% is small, but that growth is something most CFOs didn't plan for. In his view, buyers are reaching the stage where spending more is not enough and the spend has to be optimized.\n\nThat is the problem the reports address. The article also describes a second effect, which comes from Jellyfish's Nikolas Albarran. He says Anthropic's lead rests on enterprise execution and on companies having standardized workflows around its tools, and that OpenAI's Astra model has not given them enough reason to switch. Even if the tools are mostly similar, he says, each handles things like agent.md files slightly differently, so switching cost is not zero. He sees the new reports as a lighter version of the forward-deployed engineering teams the major labs embed with customers.\n\nOne caveat follows from how the reports are built: the party measuring the value of the spend is the vendor receiving it. Whether customers see the recommendations as neutral guidance is not something the article addresses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2938,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2938},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b381f5a8-dc9e-4d73-8484-6effdfbfc570","uuid":"381bc748-11e4-4f16-a6a4-cc19d7f0fe4b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:19:24.834Z","request_id":"req_011CgdY7Sg6rrRyZxTG8hcBX"}
